Store only TDATA in the TX2 conjugate delay

The TX2 conjugate and CMPY B interfaces carry no sidebands. Set the delay IP
to data-only mode so its 40 elastic stages do not store unused sideband bits.
This restores the independently elastic behavior validated at 16 clocks;
freezing every stage on one shared stall shifted the measured RF phase delay.
diff --git a/hdl/projects/pluto/system_bd.tcl b/hdl/projects/pluto/system_bd.tcl
--- a/hdl/projects/pluto/system_bd.tcl
+++ b/hdl/projects/pluto/system_bd.tcl
@@ -311,6 +311,7 @@ ad_ip_instance axis_conjugate tx2_conjugate
 ad_ip_instance axis_delay tx2_conjugate_delay
 ad_ip_parameter tx2_conjugate_delay CONFIG.DELAY_CYCLES 40
 ad_ip_parameter tx2_conjugate_delay CONFIG.DATA_WIDTH 32
+ad_ip_parameter tx2_conjugate_delay CONFIG.ENABLE_SIDEBANDS 0
 create_bd_cell -type ip -vlnv xilinx.com:ip:cmpy:6.0 rx2_tx2_cmpy
 set_property -dict [list CONFIG.FlowControl {Blocking} CONFIG.OutputWidth {16}] \
   [get_bd_cells rx2_tx2_cmpy]
